  "summary": "Bound coins cache memory growth during assumeutxo snapshot loading by bytes rather than coin count alone. The cache is now checked for flushing whenever memory usage increases by 4 MiB since the previous check, alongside the existing 120,000-coin interval.",
  "problem": "During snapshot loading in PopulateAndValidateSnapshot, cache memory is checked against -dbcache only every 120,000 coins. Because script sizes can reach 10,000 bytes, an adversarial or unusual snapshot could inflate memory usage by approximately 1.2 GB past -dbcache before triggering a flush, risking out-of-memory crashes on memory-constrained systems.",
