  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Validation snapshot loading checks coins cache limits only every 120,000 coins, which assumes typical small coin sizes. Adversarial snapshot files containing large scripts up to 10,000 bytes could cause the cache to overshoot -dbcache by roughly 1.2 GB before flushing, potentially crashing memory-limited nodes prior to snapshot hash rejection. This change triggers cache checks every 4 MiB of growth in addition to the coin count interval. The author adds a functional test with 2,000 large coins under -dbcache=4 that fails without the change.",
